 Cloud Application Programming Model is now available.   Highlights:    Revised Cookbooks and Java Documentation  Liveness and Readiness Checks for Node.js  ETag in Remote OData Services for Java  … and much more.  See March 2024 release for the CAP framework.   Action: We recommend to adapt the new versions as soon as possible, see Managing Dependencies.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-03-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3214 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: OpenTelemetry updates\nDescription: Cloud Logging now provides a dashboard for exploring OpenTelemetry metrics.  It also provides an OpenTelemetry JVM metrics dashboard.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-28\nValid as Of: 2024-03-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3215 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Boosters for SAP Document Management Service\nDescription: You can now set up the Document Management Service, Integration Option automatically using the booster from the SAP BTP cockpit itself.  For more information, see Setup Using the Booster.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-28\nValid as Of: 2024-03-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3216 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Authenticate with System as Admin\nDescription: Use access_token to authenticate a system as administrator when accessing the SCIM REST APIs. See Configure the Client to Call Identity Authentication Token Endpoint for Client Credentials Flow.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-27\nVersion: 25853\n\n--- Record 3217 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Authorizations Based on Policies\nDescription: You can configure and assign a granular control and access to applications based on custom authorization policies for the administrators of SAP Cloud Identity Services. See Configure Application Authorizations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-27\nVersion: 25853\n\n--- Record 3218 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Configure Applications\nDescription: You can view and edit the Organization ID attribute of an application. See Edit Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-27\nVersion: 25853\n\n--- Record 3219 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: External Providers\nDescription: We have changed the name of the Source System entry under Identity Providers to Authentication Provider. See Configuring External Authentication Providers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-27\nVersion: 25853\n\n--- Record 3220 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Identity Authentication has been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-27\nVersion: 25853\n\n", "--- Record 1451 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: The Project Overview is now available for CAP projects. See Project Overview.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-09\nValid as Of: 2025-02-09\nVersion: T2501a\n\n--- Record 1452 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Predictions\nDescription: In addition to anomaly detection, we have now introduced Predictions, an AI-based capability that identifies trends in API calls and predicts future API traffic. With this new capability, you can identify trends in API traffic and view predictions for upcoming API call volumes. These insights can be utilized to optimize resource allocation, manage system load, and make informed decisions about your API strategy.  See: Predictions\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1453 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tenant Cloning Tool\nDescription: The 1.9.4 version of the Tenant Cloning Tool is now available.   See: Tenant Cloning Tool Behavior    Clone API Management Content (Neo to Cloud Foundry)      Clone API Management Content between Cloud Foundry Environments      SAP API Management customers choose: Tenant Cloning Tool Behavior    Clone API Management Content (Neo to Cloud Foundry)    Clone API Management Content between Cloud Foundry Environments  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1454 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Contract References Available\nDescription: Business admins can now maintain contract references to keep an overview of the contracts you have with other business partners in a data space. Once you've created a contract reference, you can use it in policies and company policies.See Create Contract References.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1455 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.5.*      Increment: 2413      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1456 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.26.*    Increment: 2413  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1457 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.36.*      Increment: 2413    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-08\nValid as Of: 2025-02-08\nVersion: 2413\n\n--- Record 1458 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Upcoming upgrade to Kubernetes 1.31\nDescription: The Kyma environment is planned to be upgraded to the Kubernetes version 1.31 in the 2025 Q1 Maintenance and Major Upgrade Window.  For more information on the upcoming upgrade, see the feature highlights, deprecations, and removals in the blog post and the Kubernetes release notes.  See the detailed schedule for the Subaccount Regions for Kyma:  2025-02-08 14:00 - 16:00 UTC: ap10, ap12, ap21, ap20, in30, jp30  2025-02-09 07:00 - 09:00 UTC: br10, us20, us10, us11   2025-02-15 14:00 - 16:00 UTC: jp10, ap11, jp20, ap30  2025-02-15 21:00 - 23:00 UTC: e